    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kentucky Route 155, known locally as Taylorsville Road, marks Cambridge’s southern edge and leads toward Jeffersontown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge%2C_Kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "To the north, Cambridge borders Lincolnshire and St. Regis Park; to the south, it meets Houston Acres; and to the west, it abuts the city of Louisville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge%2C_Kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cambridge’s boundaries also touch the consolidated Louisville/Jefferson County on its southwest and eastern sides.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge%2C_Kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "As part of the Louisville metropolitan area, Cambridge shares the region’s economic and cultural ties while maintaining its own municipal identity.",
